From: Peter Varkoly <varkoly@suse.com>
Subject: digestmd5: fix heap overflow in add_to_challenge() when quoting

add_to_challenge() computed the needed buffer size from the unquoted
value length. When the value contains '"' or '\', quote() returns a
longer string, but the buffer was re-allocated with the stale size and
the quoted value was then appended with strcat(), overflowing the heap
buffer by an attacker-controlled amount (e.g. a crafted realm or nonce
sent by a malicious DIGEST-MD5 / HTTP Digest server).

Recompute newlen from the quoted length before re-allocating. This also
keeps *curlen consistent with the actual string length.

--- a/plugins/digestmd5.c
+++ b/plugins/digestmd5.c
@@ -567,6 +567,7 @@
 	    valuesize = strlen(quoted);
 	    /* As the quoted string is bigger, make sure we have enough
 	       space now */
+	    newlen = (unsigned) (*curlen + 1 + namesize + 2 + valuesize + 2);
 	    ret = _plug_buf_alloc(utils, str, buflen, newlen);
 	    if (ret == SASL_OK) {
 		strcat(*str, quoted);
